    "notes": "Two parts: Canto (voice, 2 stanzas = lyric numbers 1-2) and Pianoforte (ONE part, two staves - never split). Elisions (two or three syllables sung on one note, joined by the elision tie \"‿\") are a single <lyric> with <elision> between the <text> parts, e.g. \"do‿e‿al\" = text do (end) + elision + e (single) + elision + al (single). Do not split an elided group over several notes and do not drop the parts after the tie. Apostrophes (l'a-, m'in-) and accents (stò, tà, più, ché) must be kept.",
