  "truth_limitations": [
    "Truth encodes pitches, durations, rests, ties, slurs, fermatas, stem directions of voices sharing a staff, lyrics (number, syllabic, text, elision, extend) and the part/staff structure; it has no <beam>, no system or page breaks, no positions and no font sizes.",
    "Printed stanza labels (\"1.\", \"2.\" ...) are not encoded; lyric/@number carries the line number.",
    "Only title, composer, lyricist and rights are encoded from the header; subtitle and the printed poet/composer lines are not encoded as credits.",
    "LilyPond drops the hyphen when two syllables of a word are printed very close together; truth syllabic (begin/middle/end) still follows the word structure.",
    "Scan damage (pencil marks, handwritten words, stains, holes, staples, cropped margins) is not part of the truth.",
    "Elision symbols are encoded as <elision>U+203F</elision> between the text parts."
